# --- Secrets: never commit credentials into this repo ---
.env
.env.*
*.token
*.pat
*.secret
*.key
secrets/
.tokens/

# --- Local scratch (kept out of the repo) ---
node_modules/
node_modules
*.local

# ==> A ROOT package.json IS NOT OURS. <==
# §2: this project has NO BUILD STEP and no toolchain. `npm i playwright`, run
# to get the browser checks going in a cloud sandbox, drops a package.json and
# a lockfile at the root as a side effect. Committing them would put a
# dependency manifest on a static site that has none — and the next reader
# would reasonably believe there was something to install.
#
# `worker/package.json` is the ONE stated exception (§17) and is NOT matched
# here: these two patterns are anchored to the repo root with a leading slash.
/package.json
/package-lock.json

# ==> NO `vendor/` RULE. DO NOT ADD ONE BACK. <==
# `vendor/` used to be ignored as local scratch. As of SPEC §17 A3 it holds
# MapLibre and Three — SHIPPED APPLICATION CODE that index.html loads by
# path. This rule silently swallowed them on the first attempt: `git add -A`
# reported success, the commit pushed, and the deployed site served an
# index.html pointing at two files that were never uploaded. Result was a
# BLACK SCREEN — no map library, no globe, no error anybody could see.
#
# The tell was in `git status` the whole time: no `vendor/` under untracked.
# An absence is easy to not-see, which is the same failure mode §5 is about.

# --- OS / editor cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
